um levels set in Annex II","citation":"Reg. (EC) 1333/2008, Annex II — E 500","citation_url":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2008/1333/oj"}],"risk_assessment_refs":null,"usage_context":null,"source":"fda_substances_added_to_food","source_updated_at":"2026-07-28","last_full_review_at":null,"everyday_allowlist":false,"dataset_version":"2026-09-29.21b67c74"},{"id":"ing_sodium_bisulfate","canonical_name":"Sodium bisulfate","aka":[],"cas_number":null,"e_number_ins_code":null,"chemical_formula":null,"category":"other","origin":"unknown","typical_uses":["food"],"allergen_flags":[],"plain_explanation":"Notified to the US FDA as GRAS for this use: use in cake mixes as a pH control agent and a leavening agent at a level of 0.1 to 1.0 percent by weight; use in foods in general as a pH control agent and processing aid at levels not to exceed good manufacturing practices.","jurisdictions":[{"jurisdiction":"US_FDA","status":"Notified to FDA as GRAS for its intended use; FDA had no questions","citation":"GRN 3","citation_url":"https://hfpappexternal.fda.gov/scripts/fdcc/index.cfm?set=GRASNotices&id=3"}],"risk_assessment_refs":null,"usage_context":null,"source":"fda_gras_notice","source_updated_at":"2026-09-24","last_full_review_at":null,"everyday_allowlist":false,"dataset_version":"2026-09-29.21b67c74"},{"id":"ing_sodium_bisulfite","canonical_name":"Sodium bisulfite","aka":["E222","sodium hydrogen sulfite","E 222","INS 222"],"cas_number":"7631-90-5","e_number_ins_code":"E222","chemical_formula":"HNaO3S","category":"preservative","origin":"synthetic","typical_uses":["food"],"allergen_flags":["sulfites"],"plain_explanation":"A sulfite salt that releases sulfur dioxide in food, slowing browning and microbial growth.","jurisdictions":[{"jurisdiction":"US_FDA","status":"Generally Recognized as Safe (GRAS) as a chemical preservative","citation":"21 CFR 182.3739","citation_url":"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-21/section-182.3739"},{"jurisdiction":"EU_EFSA","status":"Authorised food additive; permitted foods and maximum levels set in Annex II","citation":"Reg. (EC) 1333/2008, Annex II — E 222","citation_url":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2008/1333/oj"},{"jurisdiction":"HK_CFS","status":"Permitted preservative or antioxidant; maximum levels set by food category","citation":"Cap. 132BD, Schedule 1","citation_url":"https://www.elegislation.gov.hk/hk/cap132BD!en"}],"risk_assessment_refs":["JECFA, evaluation of sulfur dioxide and sulfites — group ADI 0–0.7 mg/kg body weight"],"usage_context":{"threshold_of_concern":"Acceptable Daily Intake set at 0–0.7 mg per kg of body weight per day, as sulfur dioxide (JECFA)","typical_concentration_range":"Declarable above 10 ppm as sulfur dioxide","product_type_context":"ingested"},"source":"fda_substances_added_to_food","source_updated_at":"2026-07-28","last_full_review_at":null,"everyday_allowlist":false,"dataset_version":"2026-09-29.21b67c74"},{"id":"ing_sodium_borohydride","canonical_name":"Sodium borohydride","aka":["Sodium tetrahydroborate","Sodium borohydride (na(bh4))"],"cas_number":"16940-66-2","e_number_ins_code":null,"chemical_formula":null,"category":"flavor","origin":"unknown","typical_uses":["food"],"allergen_flags":[],"plain_explanation":"A flavouring substance, used in food to add or help carry flavour.","jurisdictions":[{"jurisdiction":"US_FDA","status":"Listed in FDA's Substances Added to Food inventory; no FDA regulation is cited","citation":"FDA Substances Added to Food","citation_url":"https://hfpappexternal.fda.gov/scripts/fdcc/index.cfm?set=FoodSubstances"}],"risk_assessment_refs":null,"usage_context":null,"source":"fda_substances_added_to_food","source_updated_at":"2026-07-28","last_full_review_at":null,"everyday_allowlist":false,"dataset_version":"2026-09-29.21b67c74"},{"id":"ing_sodium_calcium_alginate","canonical_name":"Sodium calcium alginate","aka":["Calcium sodium alginate"],"cas_number":"12698-40-7","e_number_ins_code":null,"chemical_formula":null,"category":"emulsifier","or